    "title": "feat(engine): emit an idle keep-alive sentinel during long gaps",
    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1437",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nLong thinking or long prefill leaves the SSE stream idle for many seconds. Intermediaries — proxies, load balancers, ingress controllers — have their own idle timeouts and drop the connection. To the client this shows up as a streaming 502 or a reset mid-response, with no error from vLLM itself.\n\nRaising the server-side keep-alive alone does not help: the tokens are not flowing, so no bytes are written to the stream.\n\n## Change\n\n`AsyncLLM.generate` gains an opt-in `keepalive` flag. When set, the generator emits a `STREAM_KEEPALIVE` sentinel every 15s while the internal queue is empty:\n\n```python\ntry:\n    out = await asyncio.wait_for(q.get(), timeout=_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL)\nexcept asyncio.TimeoutError:\n    yield STREAM_KEEPALIVE\n    continue\n```\n\nThe sentinel is a `RequestOutput` with `finished=False` and no outputs. Consumers must recognise it and skip it — it is not an end-of-request marker.\n\n**Why opt-in rather than always-on:** this generator has 11 call sites (chat, completion, responses, disaggregated, speech, …). Most have no logic to skip an empty output, so emitting unconditionally would corrupt their streams. Only callers that pass `keepalive=True` see it.\n\nAlso raises the default `VLLM_HTTP_TIMEOUT_KEEP_ALIVE` from 5s to 600s. A 5s server-side idle timeout drops the same long-running streams even when the sentinel keeps the response flowing.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Long thinking requests stay connected behind a proxy with a 60s idle timeout.\n- Non-keepalive callers receive an unchanged stream (verified the sentinel never appears).",
